tic.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135742133,imgsize-34218.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Louisiana appeals court revives father's will after six of his nine children challenge signatures]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135700936.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A contentious family feud arose when six of a father's nine children contested the legitimacy of his will, arguing discrepancies in signatures and the execution process. However, after legal deliberations, an appeals court overturned the initial ruling that declared the will invalid, citing insufficient evidence from the challengers. This ruling paves the way for the succession process to proceed under fresh legal stipulations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-louisiana-father-left-his-estate-to-his-wife-in-a-2015-will-but-six-of-his-nine-children-challenged-the-documents-signatures-an-appeals-court-has-reversed-a-ruling-voiding-the-will-and-ordered-further-hearings/articleshow/135700936.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-louisiana-father-left-his-estate-to-his-wife-in-a-2015-will-but-six-of-his-nine-children-challenged-the-documents-signatures-an-appeals-court-has-reversed-a-ruling-voiding-the-will-and-ordered-further-hearings/articleshow/135700936.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T20:57:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135701011,imgsize-1291145.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jane Seymour refuses to leave Malibu home despite repeated wildfire scares]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135738870.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1994-jane-seymour-bought-a-3-4-million-malibu-home-after-at-least-six-wildfire-scares-and-a-narrow-escape-in-2024-she-says-she-will-not-sell-and-has-replaced-flammable-plants-to-protect-her-oceanfront-property/articleshow/135738870.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1994-jane-seymour-bought-a-3-4-million-malibu-home-after-at-least-six-wildfire-scares-and-a-narrow-escape-in-2024-she-says-she-will-not-sell-and-has-replaced-flammable-plants-to-protect-her-oceanfront-property/articleshow/135738870.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T20:57:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135738936,imgsize-1069916.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[12-year-old girl who could barely swim survived Yemenia plane crash, clung to wreckage in Indian Ocean for hours]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135738922.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In June 2009, a tragic accident unfolded when a passenger plane plunged into the Indian Ocean near the Comoros Islands. Bahia Bakari, a brave 12-year-old girl, astonishingly survived by clinging to the wreckage for nearly 13 hours before being rescued by a sailor enduring harsh conditions. Upon recovery, she faced the heartbreaking news of her mother's death from a psychologist.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/daddy-i-couldnt-see-anything-in-2009-12-year-old-bahia-bakari-was-the-only-survivor-when-a-yemenia-plane-carrying-153-people-crashed-into-the-indian-ocean-she-could-barely-swim-but-clung-to-wreckage-for-about-13-hours-until-rescuers-arrived/articleshow/135738922.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/daddy-i-couldnt-see-anything-in-2009-12-year-old-bahia-bakari-was-the-only-survivor-when-a-yemenia-plane-carrying-153-people-crashed-into-the-indian-ocean-she-could-barely-swim-but-clung-to-wreckage-for-about-13-hours-until-rescuers-arrived/articleshow/135738922.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T20:57:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135739031,imgsize-1391583.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Germany vows action after report finds widespread sexual misconduct in military]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135740875.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/unacceptable-germany-vows-action-after-report-finds-widespread-sexual-misconduct-in-military/articleshow/135740875.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/unacceptable-germany-vows-action-after-report-finds-widespread-sexual-misconduct-in-military/articleshow/135740875.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T20:33:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135741506,imgsize-225448.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Forgotten gold coins bought in 1975 sell for £113,000 after widow finds them in shed]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135740272.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A remarkable discovery was made when a metal biscuit tin filled with 62 gold coins fetched an astonishing £113,000 at auction. Hidden for nearly five decades, these coins were acquired by a man who chose to keep his investment secret from his family during the economic struggles of the 1970s. The bidding war, fueled by interest from collectors and investors, ultimately provided substantial financial relief to his widow.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-widow-clearing-out-her-late-husbands-shed-found-a-biscuit-tin-packed-with-62-gold-coins-including-pieces-he-bought-for-70-to-80-each-in-1975-after-50-years-hidden-away-the-collection-sold-for-113000/articleshow/135740272.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-widow-clearing-out-her-late-husbands-shed-found-a-biscuit-tin-packed-with-62-gold-coins-including-pieces-he-bought-for-70-to-80-each-in-1975-after-50-years-hidden-away-the-collection-sold-for-113000/articleshow/135740272.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T20:00:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135740823,imgsize-1806140.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Tiffany Haddish's charity gives 2,000+ suitcases yearly to foster youth, inspired by her childhood]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135739362.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Drawing from her challenging childhood in the foster care system, Tiffany Haddish founded the She Ready Foundation to uplift vulnerable youth. The charity distributes thousands of suitcases yearly to children in need, collaborating with prominent brands such as Samsonite for high-grade products. Beyond luggage, the foundation focuses on career development and mentorship, with recent programs including a film project that allowed participants to learn production skills and express their creativity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2019-tiffany-haddish-founded-a-charity-inspired-by-her-years-in-foster-care-when-she-carried-her-belongings-in-trash-bags-it-now-distributes-more-than-2000-suitcases-annually-to-foster-youth/articleshow/135739362.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2019-tiffany-haddish-founded-a-charity-inspired-by-her-years-in-foster-care-when-she-carried-her-belongings-in-trash-bags-it-now-distributes-more-than-2000-suitcases-annually-to-foster-youth/articleshow/135739362.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T19:34:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135740233,imgsize-1403176.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Tech executive wins $2.75M after woman breaks $97K settlement deal with public assault claims]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135738171.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Michael Fitzgerald has been awarded $2.75 million after Ronda McNae breached a confidentiality agreement. Despite having settled with him earlier, McNae's public accusations of serious misconduct violated their pact. The court determined her actions severely harmed Fitzgerald's professional image and caused significant financial losses. The appeals court confirmed the lower court's ruling, emphasizing the impact of McNae's defamatory claims on Fitzgerald's career.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-tech-executive-paid-a-couple-97000-under-a-confidential-settlement-after-the-woman-contacted-his-employers-and-posted-assault-allegations-an-appeals-court-upheld-2-75-million-in-damages-awarded-to-him/articleshow/135738171.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-tech-executive-paid-a-couple-97000-under-a-confidential-settlement-after-the-woman-contacted-his-employers-and-posted-assault-allegations-an-appeals-court-upheld-2-75-million-in-damages-awarded-to-him/articleshow/135738171.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T18:51:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135739121,imgsize-1660819.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Blyth’s reed warbler, a small brown bird has bred in the UK for the first time]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135706561.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[For the first time in history, Blyth's reed warbler has successfully bred in the Scottish Highlands, marking a significant milestone for this species in the UK. Official confirmation comes from the Rare Breeding Birds Panel, celebrating this achievement from 2024. Additionally, various wetland bird populations are witnessing positive trends in breeding. Ongoing observation by bird enthusiasts will be crucial in ensuring future breeding achievements and maintaining population stability.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/blyths-reed-warbler-a-small-brown-bird-usually-found-from-eastern-europe-to-asia-has-bred-in-the-uk-for-the-first-time-with-a-pair-raising-chicks-in-the-highlands-according-to-a-new-rare-breeding-birds-report/articleshow/135706561.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/blyths-reed-warbler-a-small-brown-bird-usually-found-from-eastern-europe-to-asia-has-bred-in-the-uk-for-the-first-time-with-a-pair-raising-chicks-in-the-highlands-according-to-a-new-rare-breeding-birds-report/articleshow/135706561.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T20:14:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135706561,imgsize-84361.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK PM Burnham vows to unveil 10-year plan for Britain before Christmas amid Badenoch's vision jibe]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135740429.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/uk-pm-burnham-vows-to-unveil-10-year-plan-for-britain-before-christmas-amid-badenochs-vision-jibe/articleshow/135740429.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/uk-pm-burnham-vows-to-unveil-10-year-plan-for-britain-before-christmas-amid-badenochs-vision-jibe/articleshow/135740429.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T20:01:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135740857,imgsize-1084489.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘No deliberate action to unbalance election’: Brazil’s top electoral court fines Meta]]></title><description><![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/no-deliberate-action-to-unbalance-election-brazils-top-electoral-court-fines-meta-for-non-compliance/articleshow/135738897.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/no-deliberate-action-to-unbalance-election-brazils-top-electoral-court-fines-meta-for-non-compliance/articleshow/135738897.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T19:27:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135740011,imgsize-98042.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[France fears German long-range missiles could trigger nuclear escalation with Russia]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135739089.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/france-fears-german-long-range-missiles-could-trigger-nuclear-escalation-with-russia/articleshow/135739089.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/france-fears-german-long-range-missiles-could-trigger-nuclear-escalation-with-russia/articleshow/135739089.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T19:01:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135739423,imgsize-113900.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jury Awards Family $8 Million: neighbour’s ‘public nuisance’ claim rejected; boy’s care and security boosted]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135689178.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A family from San Jose has triumphantly secured an $8 million jury award after a protracted legal battle with their neighbor. The neighbor had alleged that their autistic child's vocalizations posed a public nuisance to her work life. The family argued that these sounds were a natural part of their child's condition.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-11-year-old-non-verbal-boy-with-autism-was-sued-by-a-san-jose-neighbour-who-called-his-noises-a-public-nuisance-three-years-later-a-jury-has-awarded-his-family-8-million-for-emotional-distress/articleshow/135689178.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-11-year-old-non-verbal-boy-with-autism-was-sued-by-a-san-jose-neighbour-who-called-his-noises-a-public-nuisance-three-years-later-a-jury-has-awarded-his-family-8-million-for-emotional-distress/articleshow/135689178.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T18:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135689230,imgsize-1017327.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jimmy Carter's 2,458-acre family farm in Georgia acquired for conservation; wildlife area to expand to 7,000 acres, public access planned from 2027]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135707544.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Conservation Fund has acquired the Carter family farm to protect it as wildlife habitat. Plans include opening the property to the public for outdoor activities before its state transfer. This acquisition will expand the nearby Lanahassee Creek Wildlife Management Area, enhancing conservation efforts in Georgia. The Carter family, recognizing its historical significance, supports the preservation initiative for future generations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/jimmy-carters-family-farm-in-georgia-has-been-acquired-for-conservation-nearly-2500-acres-of-fields-and-forest-are-set-to-join-a-wildlife-area-expanding-to-about-7000-acres-with-public-access-planned-from-2027/articleshow/135707544.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/jimmy-carters-family-farm-in-georgia-has-been-acquired-for-conservation-nearly-2500-acres-of-fields-and-forest-are-set-to-join-a-wildlife-area-expanding-to-about-7000-acres-with-public-access-planned-from-2027/articleshow/135707544.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T18:51:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135707781,imgsize-1620065.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian-origin Naresh Bhatt found guilty of murdering wife in US after admitting to dismembering, dumping body in trash]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135737935.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-naresh-bhatt-found-guilty-of-murdering-wife-in-us-after-admitting-to-dismembering-dumping-body-in-trash/articleshow/135737935.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-naresh-bhatt-found-guilty-of-murdering-wife-in-us-after-admitting-to-dismembering-dumping-body-in-trash/articleshow/135737935.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T18:16:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135738100,imgsize-79743.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Washington court removes $47M in damages but upholds bad-faith findings after deadly family crash]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135737539.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A recent ruling from the Washington State appeals court has slashed about $47 million in punitive damages previously awarded against Nationwide Affinity Insurance Company. This decision reaffirmed that the insurer acted in bad faith while managing claims tied to a devastating car accident. Meseret Shiferaw, who tragically lost three children in the 2017 crash, raised claims of negligence involving the insurer's handling.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-washington-mother-lost-her-three-children-in-a-2017-crash-then-her-husband-had-to-sue-her-after-an-insurance-dispute-an-appeals-court-has-now-erased-47-million-in-punitive-damages-but-upheld-other-awards/articleshow/135737539.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-washington-mother-lost-her-three-children-in-a-2017-crash-then-her-husband-had-to-sue-her-after-an-insurance-dispute-an-appeals-court-has-now-erased-47-million-in-punitive-damages-but-upheld-other-awards/articleshow/135737539.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T18:16:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135738094,imgsize-1754785.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Harry Styles' tote bag moment raises $40K for charity, funding 1,300 therapy sessions]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135737085.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Photographed in London, Harry Styles carried a tote bag linked to a cause close to the heart—mental health support. Founded by Elena Kilgore, The Other People Fund provides essential therapy sessions for individuals in need. Initially kicking off as a small clothing project, the initiative garnered remarkable attention from Styles' fanbase, raising an impressive $40,000, equating to around 1,300 affordable therapy sessions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/harry-styles-was-photographed-carrying-a-small-charitys-tote-bag-the-publicity-helped-generate-40000-in-sales-and-the-project-has-since-funded-1300-therapy-sessions-for-people-struggling-to-pay-for-care/articleshow/135737085.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/harry-styles-was-photographed-carrying-a-small-charitys-tote-bag-the-publicity-helped-generate-40000-in-sales-and-the-project-has-since-funded-1300-therapy-sessions-for-people-struggling-to-pay-for-care/articleshow/135737085.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T17:56:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135737408,imgsize-1819731.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jeremy Renner’s former Hollywood Hills land becomes $99M mansion]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https: